Language English
Debug Off

Book Journal Ordered Keep Looped
	Triggered By @ReadJournal
	
    Page Page1
        Prolog """
			The book looks new. When you flip through it, you see that there
			are only a few entries. The first one is from last Sunday.
		"""
		
        Button "Read the first Page" After "Page 1"

        Text """
            Sunday the 25th of October 1925
        
            I've decided to record what happens this week. After three
			generations of Smythes making the attempt, I think the Master will
			finally bring Our God into this world. This time, there will be no
			mistakes. His uncle failed 10 years ago, but the Master will not.
			We are gathering supplies, preparing the altar, and looking for the
			right people to help us. We will sacrifice His son in the ritual.
			He says it is painful to think about--His son is so young--but that
			is what sacrifice is. The Master is a great man.
        
            Monday the 26th of October 1925
        
            The Master told us that we may all die in the ritual. The hunger
			of Our God’s arrival will drain us. But he thinks we can supply Its
			Greatness from another source. I hired a local cleaning company to
			come to the house the day of the ritual. They should protect us.
        """
    End Page Page1

    Page Page2
        Prolog """
			You are shocked to learn that you are here to protect their lives.
			You are determined to stop them from killing you.
		"""
        
		Button "Read the next page" After "Page 2"

        Text """
            Tuesday the 27th of October 1925
    
            Preparations continue. The ritual will test the Master and maybe
			break him. He counts on the healing stone to see him through
			but one of the church members lost it. The Master told me he will
			use her instead. He said it wasn’t much of a sacrifice, but it
			would be enough when the time comes.
    
    
            Wednesday the 28th of October 1925
    
            The Master has prepared his son all week. The boy is isolated.
			The Master says his son’s fear will provide the power needed to
			create the gate.
    
            The boy's screaming kept me awake last night. It hurts to hear, but
			the Master told me this morning that power is drawing into him,
			making him stronger for Saturday.
        """
    End Page Page2

    Page Page3
        Prolog "<i>Sacrifice? His own son?!</i> These people must be stopped."
		
        Button "Read next page" After "Page 3"

        Text """
            Thursday the 29th of October 1925
    
            Kids broke into the house yesterday. One of the Brothers chased
			them off, but not before they broke into the basement. We secured
			the door with a special lock and cast a living darkness spell on
			the room. I piled boxes in front of the entrance to the place of
			power beneath the house. No one will find their way to the altar
			before Saturday.
        """

        readAboutExploreDungeonCaveViaBasement = true
        Trigger @ReadAboutExploreDungeonCaveViaBasement
    End Page Page3
 
    Page Page4
        Prolog "There are two more entries. These people must be stopped."
		
        Button "Read next page" After "Page 4"

        Text """
            Friday the 30th of October 1925
    
            The cleaning crew will be here tomorrow. Everything is prepared
			for the ritual; I can feel the excitement and fear building in
			all of us. Soon the world will belong to the One True God.
    
            The Master's son continues to plead for his life during the day,
			then screams in the night, though we don't know how he knows which
			is which. The Master told me in confidence that he yearns to stop,
			but that he must keep his commitment and see this through.
            
            The boy has been moved to the dungeon outside the altar room.
			There is a hole in the wall that he stares through when he's not
			begging or screaming. The altar is visible through the hole;
			looking at it terrifies the boy. I can no longer hear him, but I
			can still feel his fear, even across town. I will be strong.
        """
		
		readAboutBoy = true
		Trigger @PlaceExploreAltarViaCell
    End Page Page4
    
    Page Page5
        Prolog """
			You are here to feed their god. <<We must stop this horror,>> you
		    say aloud.
		"""
		
        Button "Read next page" After "Page 5"

        Text """
            Saturday the 31st of October 1925
        
            All the preparations are made. Tonight we will bring Its glory to
			this world.
        
            Earlier, the Master told me that something is bothering him,
			but he isn't sure what. He said something has changed, like there
            is another power in the house. The brethren searched by can find
			nothing.
        
            The woman who lost the stone is already at the altar. Her husband
			pleaded with me to help him find the stone; I'm going to search the
			chapel one more time. For his sake, I hope I find it.
        
            The cleaning crew should be there soon. It is time.
        """
    End Page Page5
   
    Epilog
        Text """
			This evil must be stopped. Now you know when and where the ritual
			will take place. You must hurry.
		"""
    End Epilog
End Book Journal

